{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfdCJBwawgto7AekErSma","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The candidate passed the self-check (`check_candidate` printed `OK`). It is called `complement_symmetry_aversion`.\n\n**Hypothesis:** people see a sequence of four or more flips that equals itself reversed with heads and tails swapped as deliberately built, so it looks less random by a shared weight. Examples are HHTT, TTTTHHHH, HHTTHHTT, HHHTHTTT and HTHTHTHT. Everything else is the current best model's judgement (`asymmetric_tolerance_lopsided_stretch`) unchanged. That model penalises palindromes but not this second kind of symmetry. Two-flip sequences like HT are excluded because they meet the definition trivially.\n\n**Why this cue:** I compared the best model's predictions with the observed choice rates on each of the 190 stimulus pairs. Of the features I tried, this symmetry lined up best with the leftover error, at a correlation of −0.17 (z ≈ −2.3). For example:\n- HHTT vs THHT: observed 3% vs predicted 16%.\n- TTTTHHHH vs THHHHHHT: observed 15% vs predicted 33%.\n- HTHTHTHT vs HHTHHTHH: observed 15% vs predicted 31%.\n\nThis is a single exploratory screen over about a dozen candidate features, so it is suggestive rather than confirmed.\n\n**Check result:** the smoke fit gave ELPD-LOO −3470.6, against −3500.3 for the incumbent. That fit was 100 draws on one chain, so it could not verify convergence, and its PSIS-LOO was flagged unreliable (9.4% of trials had high Pareto-k). It is not a real comparison. The check also doesn't test novelty against the other models. The effect falls only on even-length symmetric sequences, so whether it clears the 0.002 novelty threshold depends on how large the fitted weight turns out to be.\n\nI didn't take on the critique's one flagged problem (participants' left/right preferences vary more than the model produces). It doesn't survive the false-discovery correction (q = 0.128), and side-bias models are already in the set and have lost.\n\nFiles are in `…/experiment3/model_loop/iter_1/candidate_2/`:\n- hypothesis.md\n- model_name.txt\n- candidate.py"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2543,"cache_read_input_tokens":87028,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2543,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d71f3108-8581-433b-aea9-7f131de2ec33","uuid":"03ea33a9-ae16-4f59-969e-d9e5d6ac6e0b","timestamp":"2026-10-02T09:45:08.949Z","request_id":"req_011CfdCJArM8mYq3Pv5Fc2ys"}
